2","children":"GeyserMC packet translation, Floodgate authentication tokens, and why teenagers run better networks than enterprise startups."}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-12","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-12 items-start","children":[["$","aside",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-3 lg:sticky lg:top-24 space-y-8 font-mono text-xs border-b lg:border-b-0 lg:border-r border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 pb-8 lg:pb-0 pr-0 lg:pr-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[10px] text-accent font-bold uppercase tracking-widest","children":"CHAPTER OUTLINE"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2 text-ink-dark/80 dark:text-paper-200/80 text-[11px]","children":[["$","li","the-protocol-chasm",{"className":"hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#the-protocol-chasm","className":"block leading-snug","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-mono mr-1.5","children":["0",1,"."]}],"I. The Protocol Chasm"]}]}],["$","li","geyser-and-floodgate",{"className":"hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#geyser-and-floodgate","className":"block leading-snug","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-mono mr-1.5","children":["0",2,"."]}],"II. Geyser, Floodgate, and Packet Translation"]}]}],["$","li","the-relentless-20-tps",{"className":"hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#the-relentless-20-tps","className":"block leading-snug","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-mono mr-1.5","children":["0",3,"."]}],"III. The Relentless 20 TPS"]}]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-2 pt-4 border-t border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 text-[10px] text-ink-muted","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":["AUTHOR: ","Matthew Chen"," (","陳軍宇",")"]}],["$","div",null,{"children":["LOCATION: ","Jiuru / Tamsui, Taiwan"]}],["$","div",null,{"children":["MOOD: ",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold uppercase","children":"Observant"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"pt-2","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/Ch3nOff","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","className":"underline hover:text-accent","children":"GitHub @Ch3nOff"}]}]]}]]}],["$","main",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-6 space-y-12","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"drop-cap font-sans text-lg sm:text-xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-100 leading-relaxed font-light","children":"In academic computer science, distributed systems are taught with sterile diagrams: Node A sends a SYN packet, Node B acknowledges, a Raft leader is elected. It feels clean. In reality, distributed systems are chaotic, messy, and prone to silent failures — a reality any sixteen-year-old running a Paper/Spigot server network understands on an instinctual level."}],[["$","section","0",{"id":"the-protocol-chasm","className":"space-y-6 pt-4 scroll-mt-28","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 tracking-tight border-b border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 pb-2","children":"I. The Protocol Chasm"}],"$undefined",[["$","p","0",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"Consider what happens when you enable cross-play between Minecraft Java Edition and Minecraft Bedrock Edition. Java runs over TCP, expecting guaranteed in-order delivery and server-authoritative world states. Bedrock runs on mobile phones, tablets, and consoles over RakNet (UDP), relying heavily on optimistic client-side prediction."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"You are attempting to make two fundamentally contradictory networking philosophies agree on where an arrow landed in a three-dimensional voxel grid."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:hidden p-3 bg-accent/5 border-l-2 border-accent font-hand text-accent text-sm","children":["Note: ","TCP wants certainty. UDP wants speed. Bridging them is an act of diplomatic acrobatics."]}]]}],["$","section","1",{"id":"geyser-and-floodgate","className":"space-y-6 pt-4 scroll-mt-28","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 tracking-tight border-b border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 pb-2","children":"II. Geyser, Floodgate, and Packet Translation"}],"$undefined",[["$","p","0",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"This is where GeyserMC and Floodgate step in. Geyser acts as an on-the-fly protocol proxy, translating incoming RakNet packets into Java Netty byte buffers in real-time. If a Bedrock player looks at an inventory GUI, Geyser must forge fake window packets so the Java server doesn't disconnect them for packet spoofing."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"Floodgate solves the authentication identity problem: it intercepts the login sequence, cryptographically validates the Xbox Live token, and synthesizes a legitimate UUID that the Java authentication pipeline accepts without crying foul."}]],["$","figure",null,{"className":"my-8 py-6 border-y-2 border-accent/40 px-4 sm:px-6 bg-accent/5 dark:bg-accent/10","children":["$","blockquote",null,{"className":"font-serif italic text-xl sm:text-2xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 leading-snug","children":["“","Every network abstraction is a lie that works until packet loss exceeds eight percent.","”"]}]}],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}],["$","section","2",{"id":"the-relentless-20-tps","className":"space-y-6 pt-4 scroll-mt-28","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 tracking-tight border-b border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 pb-2","children":"III. The Relentless 20 TPS"}],"$undefined",[["$","p","0",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"A Minecraft server must process 20 ticks per second. That means you have exactly 50 milliseconds to calculate mob pathfinding, entity collisions, chunk loading, redstone circuits, and packet broadcasts."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"If your tick time climbs to 52 milliseconds, you fall behind. If you drop to 14 TPS, players notice the latency in their sword swings. Managing this taught me more about thread contention, garbage collection pauses in the JVM, and network buffer saturation than any classroom lecture ever could."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]],["$","footer",null,{"className":"pt-12 border-t border-ink-dark/20 dark:border-paper-100/20 space-y-4 font-mono text-xs","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[10px] text-accent uppercase tracking-widest font-bold","children":"[FOOTNOTES & FORMAL CITATIONS]"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-2 list-decimal list-inside text-ink-muted text-[11px]","children":[["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-100 font-sans","children":"Minecraft Java communicates via TCP streams using Netty; Minecraft Bedrock uses RakNet over UDP with client-side prediction."}]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-100 font-sans","children":"Floodgate circumvents standard online-mode UUID authentication by creating cryptographic Bedrock token handshakes."}]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"hidden lg:block lg:col-span-3 space-y-8 font-mono text-xs border-l border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 pl-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[10px] text-accent font-bold uppercase tracking-widest block","children":"MARGINALIA & NOTES"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"p-3 bg-paper-100/50 dark:bg-paper-900/50 border border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 space-y-1 relative","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[8px] text-accent uppercase tracking-widest block","children":["ANNOTATION § 0",1]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"margin-hand text-base text-accent","children":["“","TCP wants certainty. UDP wants speed. Bridging them is an act of diplomatic acrobatics.","”"]}]]}],null,null],["$","div",null,{"className":"p-4 border border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 bg-paper-100/30 text-[10px] space-y-2","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-accent uppercase font-bold tracking-widest","children":"PERSONAL DISCIPLINE"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-sans text-ink-dark/80 dark:text-paper-200/80 leading-normal","children":"All code samples and algorithmic theorems are tested on real silicon before archiving."}]]}]]}]]}]}]]}],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L4",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","article","children","$5","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L6",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L4",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","article","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L6",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[[[["$","link","0",{"rel":"stylesheet","href":"/_next/static/css/bb17e405